# Next Step Guyana: no vibe-coded UI

## Never ship
- Purple gradients (or purple-as-default theme)
- Pill-shaped buttons (`border-radius: 999px` / fully rounded CTAs)
- Fake reviews, testimonials, star ratings
- Fake metrics or vanity counters (invented user counts, growth %, “trusted by”)
- Vague Euro-startup copy (“unlock your potential”, “reimagine the future”, empty slogans)
- Emoji as icons
- Em dashes (—) or en dashes (–); use commas, periods, or "to" for ranges
- Over-the-top scroll / parallax / cursor-follow animations
- AI stock photos or AI stock copy
- Fake customer calendars or fabricated schedules presented as real

## Brand direction
- Keep navy, gold, green, real Guyana context
- Prefer real photography or existing brand assets (`logo.png`, `assets/`)
- Copy must be specific, honest, and local; if data is illustrative, say so plainly
- Motion: subtle and purposeful only (2 to 3 intentional moves max on marketing pages)

## Launch blockers (do not treat as launched until all are done)
1. Custom domain connected (DNS + hosting)
2. Favicon present on every public HTML page
3. No “Made with AI” (or similar) badge anywhere
4. Public `privacy.html` linked from the site footer
5. Public `terms.html` linked from the site footer

## Quality bar
- Make no mistakes: verify links, copy, and wiring before calling work done
- Prefer fixing root causes over decorative patches
- Student-facing app JS stays ES5-style; no em/en dashes in app copy
